## 2. Normalize and validate

The Code node:
- trims incoming values;
- requires client name, email, and project name;
- validates the email format;
- generates an `AFF-YYYYMMDD-XXXX` reference;
- adds timestamp and initial status.

The IF node separates accepted and rejected requests.

## 4. Send acknowledgement

Gmail sends the validated client a confirmation containing:
- client name;
- project name;
- generated project reference.

Select Gmail OAuth credentials before activation. Customize the subject and HTML body if needed.
